-- Deneb Dual-Line Variance Chart — DAX measures (spec rev 8, 4-field architecture)
--
-- The chart receives ONLY four fields from the table DualLineVariance_Workshop_Data
-- (or the user's own fact table with a Category/month column):
--   Category      column  (Sort by column -> Sort_Order so rows arrive in month order)
--   Actual        Sum of the Actual column      (rename the value well chip "Sum of Actual" to "Actual")
--   Reference     Sum of the Reference column   (rename the chip to "Reference")
--   Business_Type measure below                 ('Higher is Good' or 'Lower is Good', exact spelling)
-- The variance area, crossing points and Good/Bad colours are computed inside the spec.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- REQUIRED: the fourth field of the chart
Business_Type =
"Higher is Good"

-- To flip the meaning (lower is better, e.g. cost, defects) change the text to:
--   Business_Type = "Lower is Good"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Table: DualLineVariance_Workshop_Data (measures for other visuals)

Total Actual =
SUM ( DualLineVariance_Workshop_Data[Actual] )

Total Reference =
SUM ( DualLineVariance_Workshop_Data[Reference] )

Variance =
[Total Actual] - [Total Reference]

Variance % =
DIVIDE ( [Variance], [Total Reference] )

-- Achievement % follows the Business_Type direction, not a hardcoded "higher is better".
-- This measure is illustrative only (for a KPI card); the chart itself reads Business_Type.
Achievement % =
VAR BusinessType = [Business_Type]
VAR RawRatio = DIVIDE ( [Total Actual], [Total Reference] )
RETURN
    IF ( BusinessType = "Lower is Good", DIVIDE ( [Total Reference], [Total Actual] ), RawRatio )
